            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Over the last 15 years ultrasound has gained importance for the clinical management of patients with inflammatory rheumatic diseases, especially rheumatoid arthritis. This review summarizes the recent developments and achievements in the use of ultrasound in RA, as well as the unmet needs.</AbstractText>
